---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base description="Saramsha Dotel — software engineer in New York.">
  <section class="hero">
    <img
      class="hero-photo"
      src="/assets/img/aboutimg.jpg"
      alt="Saramsha Dotel"
      width="104"
      height="104"
    />
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1 class="hero-greeting">Hi, I'm Saramsha.</h1>
      <p class="hero-role">Applied AI Engineer | ex-Founder </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p>
    I'm a senior software engineer on the Applied AI team at <a href="https://www.wbd.com">Warner Bros. Discovery</a>. Currently, I am working
    on building a semantic search and retrieval system across our roughly million hours of film
    and TV, and an org-wide AI agent for the Media Supply Chain team that handles tasks, automates workflows, and answers questions from the customers.
  </p>

  <p>
    Before this, I was a startup co-founder. I spent five years building <a href="https://www.naamche.com">Naamche</a>,
    a software development studio I co-founded with my friends in 2020. Based out of Nepal, we grew
    it from three engineers to forty and shipped real-estate, fintech, and
    agri-tech products for clients, mostly in the US. In December 2023 we were
    <a href="https://finance.yahoo.com/news/realpha-tech-corp-acquire-naamche-120000261.html">acquired</a>
    by <a href="https://www.realpha.com">reAlpha</a>, a Nasdaq-listed proptech
    company. This was the first time a Nepali software company had been acquired by a
    Nasdaq-listed public company. I stayed at reAlpha as a tech lead for a few months
    before moving to WBD.
  </p>

  <p>
    Even before, I started my career as a machine learning engineer at
    <a href="https://fusemachines.com/">Fusemachines</a> straight out of college. I studied computer
    engineering at <a href="https://pcampus.edu.np/">Pulchowk Campus</a>,
    Tribhuvan University, in Nepal — I grew up there, and moved to New York
    for work.
  </p>

  <p>
    I read a lot and watch too much football. Mostly Liverpool.
  </p>
</Base>
